<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sindhudurg district</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sindhudurg district is the southernmost district of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konkan-coast">Konkan coast</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goa">Goa</a>, with its headquarters at Oros. It was formed in 1981 from the southern part of Ratnagiri district and is named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a>'s sea fort of Sindhudurg off Malvan. Its territory includes the former princely state of Sawantwadi.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sindhudurg-district.jpg" alt="Sindhudurg district" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ankur Panchbudhe from Pune, India · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Queen%27s_beach_(Sindhudurg_fort)_(5363549355).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
